<title>AUSTRIA: IRAQI OIL CONTRACT SIGNINGS SEEN UNLIKELY AT OPEC.</title>
<headline>IRAQI OIL CONTRACT SIGNINGS SEEN UNLIKELY AT OPEC.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq is highly unlikely to sign any oil sale contracts under the second phase of the U.N. oil-for-food plan during this week's OPEC conference, delegates said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>While traders from many oil companies were in Vienna during the producer group's meeting in November, they were noticeably absent in number at this meeting.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, Iraqi oil minister Amir Muhammad Rasheed said Iraqi oil would start flowing again once an aid distribution plan had been finalised with the United Nations, expected to be within 10 days.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
